[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:A Private Conversation]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:09.77]Why did the writer complain to the people behind him? | 作者为什么向坐在他身后的人抱怨？
[00:15.91]Last week I went to the theatre. | 上星期我去看戏。
[00:19.39]I had a very good seat. | 我的座位很好。
[00:22.07]The play was very interesting. | 戏很有意思。
[00:25.10]I did not enjoy it. | 我却无法欣赏。
[00:27.43]A young man and a young woman were sitting behind me. | 一个青年男子和一个青年女子坐在我身后。
[00:31.96]They were talking loudly. | 他们大声地说着话。
[00:34.59]I got very angry. | 我非常生气。
[00:37.41]I could not hear the actors. | 我听不见演员在说什么。
[00:40.64]I turned round. | 我回过头去。
[00:42.80]I looked at the man and the woman angrily. | 我愤怒地看着那一男一女。
[00:47.27]They did not pay any attention. | 他们毫不理会。
[00:50.69]In the end, I could not bear it. | 最后，我忍不住了。
[00:54.98]I turned round again. | 我又一次回过头去。
[00:57.75]'I can't hear a word!' I said angrily. | “我一个字也听不见！”我愤怒地说。
[01:03.45]'It's none of your business,' | “这不关你的事，”
[01:06.27]the young man said rudely. | 那青年男子粗鲁地说。
[01:09.00]'This is a private conversation!' | “这是私人谈话！”
